course: dictionary
lesson: 4064
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Read the sentence around the word, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «Ladies and gentlemen, welcome to the show!» Here gentlemen is a polite way to say men. The speaker is talking to a whole crowd, so the word is friendly and respectful.
explain: «The Stranger-man is adopted into the Tribe because he was a gentleman about the mud.» Here gentleman means a man who is kind, honest and has good manners. He behaved fairly and politely, even when things got messy.
fact: A gentleman is a polite word for a man.
fact: A gentleman is also a man who is kind, honest and has good manners.
fact: Long ago, a gentleman was a rich man from a high-class family who did not need to work.
fact: «Ladies and gentlemen» is a polite way to greet a crowd.
fact: In the UK, the sign «Gents» shows the men's toilet.
exercise: «Ladies and gentlemen, please take your seats.» What does gentlemen mean here? | *Men, said politely | Kind and honest people with good manners | Rich people who never have to work | Young children
exercise: «He behaved like a gentleman about the mud, so he was fair and kind.» What does gentleman mean in this sentence? | A small animal that lives in mud | *A man with good manners who is kind and honest | A polite word for a man | A man who never works
exercise: On a door in the UK, the sign «Gents» shows which room? | The car park | The bus stop | *The men's toilet | The ladies' café
test: «This gentleman is waiting for a taxi.» What does gentleman mean here? | A tired sailor | A ghost | A rich lord from long ago | *A polite way to say a man
test: In an old story, «a gentleman who did not need to work» is a man who is? | A shopkeeper who works every day | *A rich man from a high-class family | Lazy and cross | A friendly dog
exam: Jayden reads «a real gentleman» in a story and thinks it only means a rich man. What is the best answer? | Gentleman always means a rich man, so Jayden is right | *Gentleman can mean a kind, honest man with good manners, so the story may mean a good person | Gentleman is only a sign on a door | Gentleman means a dog that lives on a farm
